# Captured MUD2 wire frames. A .c1 file holds the server's own bytes - about a third of them are
# C1 codes above 0x7F - so it is the one thing in this repo that is NOT ASCII, and git must not
# touch it. core.autocrlf is true here, and an end-of-line conversion applied to captured evidence
# would silently rewrite the frames these fixtures exist to pin. `binary` is -text -diff -merge:
# no conversion, no textual diff, and never an automatic merge of two captures.
#
# The operator's own play sessions are never committed. A test that needs real bytes commits a
# REDACTED cut, declared by name in its test project: server->client frames only (no tx records),
# only the frames under test, who-list and other frames carrying player names dropped, nothing
# identifying. It never skips when the file is absent.
*.c1 binary
